updates.txt pass 17.

THE PATTERN THAT KEEPS RECURRING, stated as plainly as I can:
three of the six lines this pass were repeats, and every one repeated because I
had been adjusting a PARAMETER when the answer was a different QUANTITY.

  'make the name brighter'  -> I changed the colour, three times. The dots were
    already #ffffff; there is nothing lighter. The grey was ink COVERAGE: 1px
    dots on a 2px pitch is 25% fill, so white averages to mid grey. size
    gap-1 -> gap-0.4 took it to 64%.
  'gradient hard to spot'   -> would have been 'brighten the gradient'. The
    sweep is background-clip:text, so it can only paint inside glyphs. Thin
    strokes give it no area. font-extrabold is the fix.
  'stop the rainbow'        -> I picked nicer colours, twice. The complaint was
    DISPARITY, which is stop-to-stop distance, not stop quality. 180deg of hue
    -> 60deg.

In all three the user's own words named the right quantity and I substituted a
nearby one I knew how to change. Coverage vs colour. Stroke area vs saturation.
Hue distance vs hue choice. Before reaching for the obvious knob, ask what
physical quantity the complaint is actually about.

Also worth keeping: 'apply a glow BEHIND it' was not a restatement of the glow
already present. shadowBlur glows each dot and drop-shadow traces the word's
outline; neither puts light on the BACKGROUND the letters sit on. A preposition
in a request can be the whole specification.

